# WOR-310 Phase B intentionally drops the ``USER worthless`` directive
# so deploy/start.py can run as root briefly, resolve the two service
# uids (worthless-proxy=10001, worthless-crypto=10002), chown the
# share files, and call setresuid before exec'ing uvicorn.  Dockle's
# CIS-DI-0001 check ("last user should not be root") sees the
# image-default and fires WARN — but the runtime never actually runs
# as root past the priv-drop dance.  The runtime security claim is
# verified by the two-uid integration tests in
# tests/test_install_docker.py and the priv-drop unit suite in
# tests/cli/test_sidecar_lifecycle_priv_drop.py.
CIS-DI-0001

# worthless-tw1g: the Debian 13 base (python:3.13-slim-trixie) clears its
# package lists with `apt-get dist-clean`, where the Debian 12 base used
# `rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists`.  Dockle's DKL-DI-0005 pattern-matches the
# older command in the layer history and does not recognise `dist-clean`,
# so it fires FATAL on a base-image layer we do not author.
#
# The check is satisfied in substance, MEASURED 2026-09-08 inside the built
# amd64 image:  `ls -A /var/lib/apt/lists/` is EMPTY.  Our own two RUN
# layers additionally end in `rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*` (Dockerfile:10,
# Dockerfile:19), so nothing we add reintroduces a cache.
#
# What remains is `/var/cache/apt/archives/lock` — a zero-byte lockfile, not
# a package cache.
#
# Remove this entry if Dockle learns `apt-get dist-clean`, or if the base
# reverts to the older idiom.
DKL-DI-0005
